Signal Check — AI Mock Interview Coach
Day 40/60 — #60DaysOfClaudeAI
A single-file, zero-dependency web app that runs a 3-question mock interview and gives structured, honest feedback on every answer — plus a live "readiness" score you can watch fill up like a studio VU meter.
What it does
Takes a target role (e.g. Frontend Developer Intern)
Asks one behavioral, one technical, and one situational/deeper question, one at a time
Scores each answer 0–100 with a verdict, strengths, gaps, and a rewritten "stronger version" of your own answer
Ends with an overall readiness score and a single top priority to fix before your next real interview
Why it looks like this
The UI borrows from a recording studio instead of a generic chat box — a circular readiness dial, a signal-chain style eyebrow label, and a strict type split: monospace for anything measured (scores, question numbers, labels) and a display face for anything spoken (questions, feedback). The metaphor: this tool is measuring the signal in a spoken answer.
Tech
Pure HTML/CSS/JS, single file, zero external libraries or CDN fonts
Live version calls the Claude API (claude-sonnet-4-6) with a strict JSON-only system prompt covering three actions: question, evaluate, summary
This build ships in demo mode — a fully pre-written session (role, answers, feedback) runs end-to-end on clicks alone, so it's reliable for screen recording with no network dependency
Built-in "How this was built" panel documents the system prompt design and extension ideas (tools, memory, voice input via Web Speech API)
Run it
Open the HTML file in any browser. No build step, no install.
Built as part of the #60DaysOfClaudeAI challenge by @abtalksonai — one polished app a day, in public.
